# CAPSHOT environment variables (Phase 1 Plan 03).
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) for local dev. For production
# deploys, set these in the Vercel dashboard: Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables. The server-side vars must be marked NOT available
# in the browser (uncheck "Available in browser" on Vercel).
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-side (public — ships in bundle). Pixel IDs are NOT secrets per Meta
# docs — they are published in every Pixel-enabled site's HTML. Set this via
# `VITE_` prefix so Vite inlines it into dist/ at build time.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_META_PIXEL_ID=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side ONLY (never prefix with VITE_). These power api/track-lead.ts,
# which posts to Meta's Conversions API. If either is missing, the edge
# function responds 200 with {skipped:true, reason:'env-missing'} so client
# fetches never reject — graceful degradation.
#
# META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN: Meta Events Manager → Data Sources → [Pixel] →
#   Settings → Conversions API → Generate access token
# META_CAPI_DATASET_ID: Meta Events Manager → Data Sources — same ID as the
#   Pixel ID for standard setups; CAPI dataset is the same as Pixel for Lead
#   events in Phase 1.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN=
META_CAPI_DATASET_ID=
